d to  discuss some background info from the  manga to put it simply in this world as  long as people still fear something then  a devil representing that thing will  always be born again what this means is  that when the devil is killed on earth  like the bat devil was then his spirit  will be reincarnated down in hell with  no memories from his previous life in  that way the devil gains a whole new  personality and if it ever returns to  earth and it can end up acting  drastically different from what it used  to be when it comes to the bat devil  this was one of those cases because when  he naturally reappeared after denji  killed him he became a brainless Savage  who couldn't talk and whose only  Instinct was to kill whoever happened to  be in front of him anyway switching over  to the octopus devil this animal has a  contract with Yoshida who's a private  devil Hunter and high school student  during his appearances so far Yoshida  has proven to be highly skilled in  combat and is able to incorporate devil  Powers into his fighting style for  instance in chapter 61 he strategically  summoned the octopus Devils just before  he took a huge hit and then after he was  thrown backwards its massive tentacles  were there to protect him following that  the devil sprayed large amounts of ink  which covered the room in darkness  giving ashita the chance to briefly  sneak through the Shadows undetected  against most enemies this would give him  the advantage especially since he can  then summon multiple giant tentacles at  the same time these tentacles can be  used to effortlessly deal with large  crowds or they can be used to restrain  someone and teleport them to a different  location something we see Yoshida do in  chapter 110 in order to summon the  octopus though he needs to make a hand  symbol by Crossing his two fingers  together similar to how certain other  Devils require hand gestures to be  summoned as well Additionally the  octopus devil is independent enough to 